--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Interoperability and scope
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

RevLink Sidecar exists to solve one problem: an AccessPort stores your
datalogs and maps over USB, but it only talks to a Windows PC or a Mac. This
project lets the owner of an AccessPort reach their own files from a phone,
without a laptop. It is a companion to that hardware, not a replacement for
it, and not a competitor to any vendor's tuning products or services.

The file-transfer protocol implemented here was determined by observing USB
traffic between an AccessPort and its own host software, on hardware owned by
the author, for the sole purpose of interoperating with that hardware.

What this project does NOT contain and does NOT do:

  * It contains no COBB source code, firmware, calibration data, map content,
    vehicle definitions, or other protected material. The part-number table in
    firmware/components/accessport_catalog is a list of publicly published
    product identifiers and the car brand each is sold for; see
    docs/ACCESSPORT_CATALOG.md.

  * It does not decode, unlock, or convert protected or vendor-locked map
    formats, and there is no plan to. Tuners protect maps deliberately, and
    this project reads only the metadata a map file publishes about itself.

  * It does not flash ECUs, perform real-time tuning, or interpret or generate
    calibration data. Those are permanently out of scope.

  * It does not modify, patch, redistribute, emulate, or circumvent any vendor
    software, licensing, device activation, or vehicle marrying/unmarrying
    process.

  * It does not extract calibration data from a vehicle.

  * It reads and writes ordinary files on hardware the user already owns.
    Published images can write and delete files on that hardware, but both
    arrive locked behind separate owner consents; see SAFETY.md.

Modifying a vehicle may affect its warranty, emissions compliance, and legal
road status. Using this software is the user's own responsibility, and it is
provided without warranty of any kind.

